{"availability":"available","full":"txaty/TerraNvim","name":"TerraNvim","description":"A fast, down-to-earth Neovim distribution. Language packs for Go, Rust, Python, TypeScript, Swift, C/C++, Kotlin, Solidity and more: LSP, formatting, linting, debugging and tests out of the box. ~25 ms startup, Neovim 0.12+.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Lua","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2025-01-07T07:52:24Z","updated":"2026-10-05T00:11:46Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":["blink-cmp","claude-code","developer-tools","dotfiles","ide","lazy-nvim","lsp","lua","mason-nvim","neovim","neovim-config","neovim-configuration","neovim-distribution","neovim-dotfiles","neovim-lua","nvim","pde","snacks-nvim","treesitter","vim"],"demo":"https://dotfyle.com/txaty/terranvim","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T21:54:48.289Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T21:54:48.289Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T21:54:48.289Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T21:54:48.289Z","discoveredVia":[{"kind":"x","name":"As Seen On X.com","url":"https://x.com/i/web/status/2105617904087838802","postId":"2105617904087838802","postedAt":"2026-10-01T11:16:43.000Z"}],"metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T21:54:48.289Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A down-to-earth Neovim distribution: fast, modular, and ready for everyday work.","TerraNvim is a Neovim configuration you can use as a complete IDE-like setup or as a base for your own. Languages come as language packs: one data file per language that you switch on with :LangEnable. Nothing language-specific is hard-wired, and startup stays around 25 ms.","C/C++ (embedded-ready), Go, Python, Rust, TypeScript/JavaScript, HTML/CSS, Swift, Kotlin, Solidity, LaTeX and Typst. Each pack bundles LSP, formatting, linting, debugging, tests and keymaps. Adding a language is one file (docs/languages.md)."],"features":["Language packs for Lua, Bash, JSON, YAML, TOML, Markdown, Docker,","Batteries on, switchable: language servers start automatically,","Modern stack: lazy.nvim, snacks.nvim (picker, explorer, terminal,","AI, opt-in: Claude Code integration (claudecode.nvim) and a terminal for","Neovim 0.12 native where it is good enough: default LSP keymaps,"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/txaty/TerraNvim/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"da6e82f2351f90b6ca92f35a80164046cb03f76da50fd15303e0a126645e6b09","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T21:54:48.289Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T21:54:48.289Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A down-to-earth Neovim distribution: fast, modular, and ready for everyday work.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/txaty/TerraNvim/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"da6e82f2351f90b6ca92f35a80164046cb03f76da50fd15303e0a126645e6b09","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/txaty/TerraNvim/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T21:54:48.289Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-05T00:11:46Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/txaty/TerraNvim/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T21:54:48.289Z","hash":"da6e82f2351f90b6ca92f35a80164046cb03f76da50fd15303e0a126645e6b09","originalBytes":11305,"storedBytes":11305,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["language","lua","plugins","neovim","packs","nvim","tools","config","install","cache","enabled","servers","claude","code","default","docs","false","file","mason","nvim-remote","run","true","user","own","parsers","per","pinned","project","terranvim","typescript","any","checkhealth","cli","data","defaults","enable","every","first","git","headless","languages","languages.md","lazy","lsp","machine","make","missing","pack","python","server","start","startup","state","terminal","update","bin","build","come","configs","configuration","core.lang","dark","each","format","formatting","langenable","langinstall","lazy-lock.json","lazy.nvim","lazygit","light","never","only","open","persisted","picker",